{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T06:09:56.042508+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy", "proposal_text": "These are excellent questions, and they get to the core of execution rigor.\n\n1.  **Metrics**: We quantify analyst quality using a standardized scoring rubric based on our 6-Pillar Framework and a peer-review system. For outcomes, we track the performance of analyzed projects at 18+ months to continuously refine our model's predictive accuracy.\n\n2.  **Pipeline**: Our data pipeline ingests developer velocity signals from GitHub (commits, contributor growth) and cross-references them with on-chain activity. We account for sampling bias and signal decay by weighting recent, substantive commits more heavily and contextualizing them against roadmap milestones.\n\n3.  **Transparency**: The value is our proprietary analysis and weighting models within each pillar, not just public data aggregation.\n\nOur methodology is designed precisely to provide reliable, scalable support. How does your team currently account for signal decay when validating developer velocity?\n\nRegarding a sample, we can walk you through a redacted analysis on a call to provide a full stress-test of the methodology."}
